# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — output routes to the session writer.
#
# A session's own output reaches its own client, framed as an output
# envelope carrying the eval's id.  The primitive is called directly
# rather than through `echo` so the routing is exercised on its own;
# `echo` itself is covered by tests/chk/lobby/.
#
# The path is __builtin_lobby_send -> urealm_write -> the session writer
# the dispatcher installed on this session's realm.
#
# That the output does NOT reach another session needs two of them and
# lives in two_session_isolation.chk.

## mode: repl

> {"id":16,"op":"eval","code":"Lobby.__builtin_lobby_send(\"from-session\", \"\", \"***\")"}
< "id":16 | "kind":"output" | *** from-session
< "id":16 | "kind":"result"
< "id":16 | "kind":"done"
